Package: lindos-gaming
Version: 1.0.0
Section: games
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Lindos Team <team@lindos.dev>
Depends: lindos-core (>= 1.0.0), gamemode, mangohud, steam-devices, python3 (>= 3.10), curl | wget, flatpak, udev, procps
Recommends: steam-launcher | steam-installer, lutris, heroic, prismlauncher, antimicrox, goverlay, piper, corectrl, openrgb, mesa-vulkan-drivers, libvulkan1, vulkan-tools, xdg-desktop-portal-gtk, pciutils, mesa-utils, ubuntu-drivers-common, gnupg, zenity | yad, libnotify-bin
Suggests: dkms, linux-headers-generic, mokutil, xdg-utils, umu-launcher, lindos-compat
Homepage: https://lindos.dev
Description: Lindos gaming stack — launchers, Proton-GE, GPU drivers, GameMode, MangoHud, controllers
 Everything Lindos wires up for gaming on top of Linux Mint XFCE:
  * lindos-game    — install/inspect/launch Steam, Lutris, Heroic, Prism Launcher
                     (Minecraft Java), Sober (Roblox), Vinegar (Roblox Studio),
                     mcpelauncher (Minecraft Bedrock, unofficial) and Bottles;
                     privileged part runs through the Lindos helper
                     (/usr/libexec/lindos/install-gaming.sh).
  * lindos-proton  — download, verify (SHA-512) and install GE-Proton releases
                     for Steam and umu-launcher; list/remove versions.
  * lindos-drivers — GPU detection (lspci), driver status, NVIDIA/AMD/Intel driver
                     installation via ubuntu-drivers, nvidia-drm modeset, optional
                     xpadneo/xone controller drivers.
  * lindos-game route/play/shortcut/cloud — honest routes for the 15 titles a
                     kernel-level anti-cheat blocks on any Linux: official cloud
                     streaming (NVIDIA GeForce NOW, Xbox Cloud Gaming, Boosteroid,
                     Amazon Luna — only where the title and your region actually
                     support it) or a one-click restart into an existing Windows
                     install; never the Lindos VM and never a spoofer.
  * GameMode config (/etc/gamemode.ini) that pauses the compositor while gaming,
    MangoHud defaults (/etc/xdg/MangoHud/MangoHud.conf, Shift_R+F12),
    controller udev rules, vm.max_map_count sysctl, launcher catalogue and the
    game compatibility matrix used by Lindos Settings and docs/COMPATIBILITY.md.
 .
 Honesty notes: Windows games run through Wine/Proton (a translation layer, not
 Windows). Valorant (Vanguard) and Fortnite (Epic disabled EAC-Linux) do not run
 on any Linux, including Lindos. Roblox runs through Sober, not the Windows
 client; Minecraft Java is native. Steam titles depend on the developer enabling
 anti-cheat for Proton — see areweanticheatyet.com and protondb.com. Launchers
 are downloaded from Valve/Flathub/GitHub on demand, never in postinst.
